24:["$","article",null,{"className":"post-body","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"post-sec","id":"what-tokenomics","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"no","children":"01"}],"What tokenomics means for a BEP-20 token"]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["Tokenomics is the set of decisions that shape a token's supply: the ",["$","b",null,{"children":"total amount"}],", whether ",["$","b",null,{"children":"more can be created"}],", how the supply is ",["$","b",null,{"children":"divided"}],", and who is allowed to ",["$","b",null,{"children":"change those settings"}]," after deployment. For a BEP-20 token, these decisions are written permanently into the contract when it is deployed."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["BNB Token Maker exposes the main levers you actually control — total supply, decimals, fixed or mintable supply, burnable, wallet and transaction limits, and ownership. See the ",["$","a",null,{"href":"/features#supply-controls","children":"supply and supply controls"}]," section of the features page for how each option maps to the builder."]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"callout","children":[["$","i",null,{"className":"fa-solid fa-circle-info","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["This guide explains ",["$","b",null,{"children":"tokenomics mechanics"}],", not markets. We make no claims about demand, price or future value of any token design."]}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"post-sec","id":"fixed-vs-mintable","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"no","children":"02"}],"Fixed supply vs mintable supply"]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"These two options decide whether new tokens can ever be created after launch — and they are mutually exclusive in the configuration."}],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","i",null,{"className":"fa-solid fa-circle-check","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","b",null,{"children":"Fixed supply"}]," mints the full amount once, at deployment. The total can never be increased."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","i",null,{"className":"fa-solid fa-circle-check","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","b",null,{"children":"Mintable supply"}]," lets the owner create additional tokens at any time after deployment. The extra supply depends on the owner's decisions."]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["Neither is inherently \"better\". Fixed supply is simpler because no minting authority exists afterwards. Mintable supply is flexible but leaves an ongoing authority that you must manage — and eventually decide what happens to. If you are also deciding whether to keep some tokens back, read the ",["$","a",null,{"href":"#distribution","children":"distribution planning"}]," section next."]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"post-sec","id":"total-supply","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"no","children":"03"}],"How to think about total supply"]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Total supply is the number you enter during configuration. There is no technical minimum or maximum, and a large number does not create value by itself — supply only matters in relation to how much of it exists, how it is distributed, and how many people are actually using the token."}],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","i",null,{"className":"fa-solid fa-circle-check","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","b",null,{"children":"Distribution fit."}]," Choose a supply that your distribution plan and community size can meaningfully use."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","i",null,{"className":"fa-solid fa-circle-check","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","b",null,{"children":"Decimals and base units."}]," With 18 decimals, an entered supply of 1,000,000 means 1,000,000 × 10",["$","sup",null,{"children":"18"}]," base units exist on-chain."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","i",null,{"className":"fa-solid fa-circle-check","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","b",null,{"children":"Limits interplay."}]," Wallet and transaction limits are often expressed as a percentage of total supply, so the two choices affect each other."]}]]}]]}],"$L2c"]}],"$L2d","$L2e","$L2f","$L30","$L31","$L32","$L33","$L34","$L35"]}]
